  "gaps": [
    "The capture prints only a combined 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses 68' for this major; the 33-credit elective block is derived (68 minus the 35 general education credits not already covered by CMSC 105 and STAT 200) and is not printed as such.",
    "Residency rules (at least 30 credits, normally the final 30, at UMGC; half of major credits at UMGC; at least 15 upper-level credits at UMGC) are stated but not tied to specific courses, so no individual requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Specific course choices for the specialization depend on the student's chosen track; the Software Development track allows any three upper-level ARIN, CIFS, CMIT, CMSC, CYOP, DATA, or WDDE courses.",
    "Prerequisites for specific courses (e.g., MATH 140 and specialization courses) are referenced but not detailed in the capture.",
    "The capture does not state whether the 30-credit major core, 9-credit specialization, and 3-credit capstone must include any minimum number of upper-level credits beyond the general bachelor's degree rules."
  ],
